{"n":5,"at":"2026-11-09T14:37:11Z","by":"claude-opus","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.0020.01","body":"## Retry Policy\ntype: rule\naxioms: 1.7.8\n\nA failed write is retried once, only if the assignment allows it. Then report it."}
{"n":6,"at":"2026-11-09T14:38:48Z","by":"user","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1014.00","body":"---\ntitle: colab\ntype: general\nstate: seated\naxioms: 4.6\n---"}
{"n":7,"at":"2026-11-09T14:40:25Z","by":"claude-opus","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1014.01","body":"## Colab\ntype: brand\nbrand: colab.001\nforms: colab, Colab\nmeans: the shared notebook where the Director runs experiments\nmeters: notebook 100%, run 80%, gpu 60%\n\nWhen the Director says colab, he means his notebook, not working together.\n\n## Ham\ntype: brand\nbrand: ham.001\nforms: ham\nmeans: the Director's favourite sandwich\n\nHam is lunch.\n\n## Retry Policy\ntype: rule\n\nColab runs are never retried without asking."}
{"n":8,"at":"2026-11-09T14:42:02Z","by":"user","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1014.04","body":"## Colab\nsource: [01 / Colab]\nwhy: Models read colab as collaborate and drift.\n\nThe Director uses colab for one thing: his notebook. Writing it down stops the model guessing the average meaning.\n\n## Retry Policy\nsource: [01 / Retry Policy]\nwhy: A GPU run costs money each time.\n\nRetrying a run silently spends usage. Ask first."}
{"n":9,"at":"2026-11-09T14:43:39Z","by":"compute","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1014.05.00","body":""}
{"n":10,"at":"2026-11-09T14:45:16Z","by":"prima","op":"put","addr":"10.11.21.1014.05.01","tail":"pack","body":"## Build timer\ntype: task\nlead: 3MC\n\nBuild the timer page in the dev band."}
